problems.problem:
Dana wants to draw a circle ($C_0$) and six circles ($C_1, C_2, \ldots, C_6$) around it in such a way that:
• $C_0$ is externally tangent to $C_i$ for $i = 1, 2, \ldots, 6$;
• $C_i$ is externally tangent to $C_{i+1}$ for $i = 1, \ldots, 5$ and $C_6$ is externally tangent to $C_1$;
• the radius of $C_i$ is $a^{n_i}$, for $i = 0, 1, \ldots, 6$, where $a > 1$ and the $n_i$ are distinct non-negative integers.
Show that Dana can succeed by exhibiting a construction that works, or provide a proof that no such construction exists.
